<!-- End 1-001: Divider --> </td></tr><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-011: Scaled Image -->
<section id="1011_scaled_image" layout-row="true"><div layout-row="true"><table layout-row="true" role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <tbody><tr layout-row="true"> <td valign="top" align="center" style="padding: 0px 20px 20px 20px"> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <tbody><tr> <td align="center" style="padding: 0px 0px 0px 0px" data-groupid="scaled"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/capabilities/quantumblack/our-insights/is-that-ai-agent-worth-it-agentic-economics-and-the-modern-operating-model?__hScId__=v710000019f9344d7c494d429f4bbcfb920&__hRlId__=a62039a35ac74a7c0000021ef3a0bcd6&__hDId__=a62039a3-5ac7-4a7c-8617-a2cc300cb0f8&__hSD__=d3d3Lm1ja2luc2V5LmNvbQ==&cid=mgp_opr-eml-nsl-shl-mgp-glb--&hlkid=bb297e8030fc47f59d443cc1dc289b04&hctky=17208988&hdpid=a62039a3-5ac7-4a7c-8617-a2cc300cb0f8" data-managed-link="scaled_link_url" target="_blank" data-link-id="8c34ac01a3ab11ecacff45a63c150deb"><img agilecontent="true" src="https://images.harmony.epsilon.com/ContentHandler/images?id=eb1bdfc0-8526-11f1-bbff-fb51bd1bf548" alt="An image linking to the web page “Is that AI agent worth it?” on McKinsey.com." width="600" height="auto" style="display: block; vertical-align: top" border="0" class="wrap"></a></td> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </section> <!-- End 1-011: Scaled Image --> </td></tr><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-008: Paragraph | P1 --><section id="1008_p1" layout-row="true"><div layout-row="true"><table layout-row="true" role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <tbody><tr layout-row="true"> <td valign="top" align="left"> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="wrap"> <tbody><tr> <td align="left" style="padding: 0px 20px 20px 20px" class="pad20rl match"><p style="font-size: 14px; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 150%; margin: 0px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: 0px; text-transform: none; color: #333333; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" enable-personalization="true" data-richtext="p1_text" data-groupid="p1" class="mobile_match"><span style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 150%;"><strong>Cheaper tokens, costlier work.</strong> Ninety-three percent of respondents to a recent McKinsey survey report exceeding their AI budgets—even as the sticker price of AI keeps falling. The culprits are rework and variance: Roughly 60 percent of the cost of an agentic task goes to checking and repairing the first answer, and an identical assignment can cost 30 times more depending on the model used. Our colleagues argue that the CEO’s job is not to squeeze tokens but to <span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/capabilities/quantumblack/our-insights/is-that-ai-agent-worth-it-agentic-economics-and-the-modern-operating-model?__hScId__=v710000019f9344d7c494d429f4bbcfb920&__hRlId__=a62039a35ac74a7c0000021ef3a0bcd7&__hDId__=a62039a3-5ac7-4a7c-8617-a2cc300cb0f8&__hSD__=d3d3Lm1ja2luc2V5LmNvbQ==&cid=mgp_opr-eml-nsl-shl-mgp-glb--&hlkid=d2e4db31652947fda648ba7df0b197fa&hctky=17208988&hdpid=a62039a3-5ac7-4a7c-8617-a2cc300cb0f8" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="29be6b80852711f1b0178dde49c8033d">govern machine work</a></span>—allocating intelligence like capital and measuring agents against business outcomes, not technical metrics.&nbsp;<br><br><strong>The vanishing bottom rung.</strong> Expertise has long been forged on the bottom rung, in the routine research and first drafts that teach judgment by repetition. This is precisely the work AI now absorbs, multiplying the output of experienced people while slowing down novices, who cannot immediately tell when the machine is wrong. A third of employers say AI has already thinned the tasks juniors once learned from. But a company that dismantles the base of its pyramid will, in a decade, have nobody left to promote. In a new article, our colleagues show <span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/capabilities/people-and-organizational-performance/our-insights/building-expertise-in-the-age-of-AI-who-trains-the-next-generation?__hScId__=v710000019f9344d7c494d429f4bbcfb920&__hRlId__=a62039a35ac74a7c0000021ef3a0bcd8&__hDId__=a62039a3-5ac7-4a7c-8617-a2cc300cb0f8&__hSD__=d3d3Lm1ja2luc2V5LmNvbQ==&cid=mgp_opr-eml-nsl-shl-mgp-glb--&hlkid=7ea1dd1ebb04419a9e0075807e569e24&hctky=17208988&hdpid=a62039a3-5ac7-4a7c-8617-a2cc300cb0f8" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="3a4ed660852711f1b0178dde49c8033d">how this pipeline can be rebuilt</a></span>.<br><br>We hope you find these insights helpful. See you in a couple of weeks with more McKinsey ideas for the CEO and others in the C-suite.</span></p></td> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </section> <!-- End 1-008: Paragraph | P1 --> </td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td><table role="presentation" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="640" border="0" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="wrap"><tbody><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-001: Divider -->
